# NOTE ON A RULE THAT USED TO BE HERE: the snapshot ignore.
#
# Jest snapshots belong in version control. Ignored, a snapshot test has nothing
# to compare against, so it writes a new one and passes outside CI and refuses to
# write and fails inside it. Neither is a check.
#
# The root .gitignore had the same rule and was fixed first; this file kept it, so
# the snapshots stayed untracked and CI failed with "New snapshot was not written"
# on a branch where they had been generated locally. Sweep every ignore file in a
# repository, not just the one at the top.
